  "paulinecsamillano": {
    "timestamp": "9/3/2026 13:58:41",
    "raw_name": "Pauline C. Samillano",
    "matched_name": "Sam Harrison",
    "pin": "SHA",
    "class": "802",
    "cat1_personal": "My house, holds so many memories that will always be tied to me no matter what. Though there were times when something shouldn't be kept in my mind, I personally think that's what makes a home, a home. Not to mention the good times I've had with others in my home. \n\nSchool, It may not be something I always look forward to, but the memories that I make here, is something I could never relive. All of the times when I was with my friends, teachers, and just being here, makes me realize that this is a one time thing, and I should take every moment for granted.",
    "cat2_community": "The Commons, just being with my family, and friends there, always makes such good memories. And I enjoy every second and minute when I'm there. \n\nThe Mic Mac Mall, always going there will unlock memories I've kept in the back of my mind and have forgotten about it. Makes me feel really nostalgic when I go through each area of the place.",
    "cat3_global": "Saudi Arabia, I was born here, which would make sense with all of the older memories I've made with others. Whenever I get reminded of the place I would never forget, it always makes me feel really nice. \n\nThe Philippines, though I've never been there for long, even when I'm from there. I remember all the people I've met that I haven't seen in so long nowadays, always makes miss them a lot! Especially the place I was living at that time.",
    "cat4_aspirational": "South Korea, all of the food I've seen from there, makes my stomach grumble every time, and the place just looks gorgeous from the pictures I've seen before.\n\nGermany, I've dreamed about going there, as I don't have much information about the place. I've always wanted to learn the language as it really interest me.",
    "cat5_music": "High Hopes by Panic! At the disco, always hearing it on social media, or even on the radio always makes me think about the older memories I've created, and not to mention, it was my favorite song of all time before I started to grow older and older.",
    "youtube_url": ""
  },
