    "class": "903",
    "cat1_personal": "Cottage: My moms family has owned a cottage in Pictou for 55 years. It doesn't hold one specific memory, but I can remember going there for around a month of every summer since I could remember and it's a happy place.\n118 Highway: During covid my dad and stepmom realised we were finishing our school work quickly so they decided to make their own classes to keep us busy. I have a very vivid memory of my dad making me and my siblings act like we were military marching down the 118 for phys ed.",
    "cat2_community": "Shubie Park: This is my favorite place to take a brain break and walk my dogs.\nLake Banook. Kayaking is my favorite sport. I do year round training with some of my best friends and make my best memories at Banook.",
